From: bake
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] atexit: minimal includes for libc_nonshared members

The libc_nonshared members are compiled outside glibc's build system with
a pruned internal include chain. Replacing the header trio with stddef.h
(freestanding, provides NULL) plus forward declarations of the externals
used keeps the transitive include graph (stdlib.h → libc-lockP.h →
pthread-functions.h → setjmp.h → build-generated headers) out entirely.
Bodies are unchanged.

--- a/stdlib/atexit.c
+++ b/stdlib/atexit.c
@@ -35,9 +35,10 @@
    <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.  */
 
-#include <stdlib.h>
-#include <dso_handle.h>
-#include "exit.h"
+#include <stddef.h>
+extern int __cxa_atexit (void (*func) (void *), void *arg, void *d);
+libc_hidden_proto (__cxa_atexit);
+extern void *__dso_handle __attribute__ ((__visibility__ ("hidden")));
 
 /* Register FUNC to be executed by `exit'.  */
 int
